Cherry-picks from lwIP upstream master, applied on top of release 2.2.1.

These are not MINIX changes.  They are fixes that upstream committed after the
2.2.1 release and has not yet put in a release of its own -- upstream's own note
says "next release will probably be 2.2.2".  Being on the latest release is not
the same as being current: several of these are security fixes in code we
compile and expose to the network.

DROP THIS DIRECTORY when lwIP is next upgraded to a release that contains them
(2.2.2 or later): they will already be in dist/, and re-applying them will
fail or double-apply.  Check with:

    git log --oneline STABLE-2_2_1_RELEASE..<new tag> -- src/

The patches, oldest upstream commit first:

  0001-0003  nd6: parse *all* neighbour-discovery options rather than only the
             first, plus the follow-up cast fix and link-layer address helper.
             IPv6 ND is the area the CVEs we were exposed to lived in, and we
             build with IPv6 on.
  0004       tcp_in: bounds-check the TCP option bytes.  tcp_get_next_optbyte()
             could read past the end of the options area, which any peer can
             trigger with malformed options -- an out-of-bounds read on input.
  0005       netif: verify the hardware address length on netif add.
  0006       ip4_frag/ip6_frag: fix a NULL-pointer dereference on memory errors
             during fragment reassembly.  We build with reassembly enabled.
  0007-0008  ip4: the IP_MIN_FRAG_LENGTH and IP4_MIN_MTU_LENGTH definitions.
             Not fixes in themselves; 0009 does not build without them.
  0009       ip4/tcp: send a zero IP_ID for small packets (do not leak a
             predictable, incrementing IP ID to the network).

Selection: only fixes touching code MINIX actually builds.  Deliberately left
out are the DHCP, AutoIP, mDNS, SNMP, SMTP, TFTP and httpd fixes (we build none
of those apps), the big-endian TCP timestamp fix (x86 is little-endian), and the
sys_check_timeouts() API change (no security value, and it would churn the glue).
